{
  "module": "MWake.tla",
  "status": "refinement",
  "summary": "Wake (wake.rs), the signal a thread of the runtime waits on: a producer publishes then swaps `pending` and notifies under the lock, the one consumer re-checks `pending` under the lock before it blocks; no published value waits for the timeout, which the model does not contain. Checked against the two waiters of the default single-owner runtime, the core thread and the store worker. With --delivery-shards K >= 1 each shard worker waits on a Wake of its own with the same loop; that loop was read and has no replay.",
  "issues": [648],
  "tests": ["mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/wake.rs"],
  "replays": [{"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/wake.rs", "test": "a_signal_raised_before_the_wait_is_consumed_without_waiting"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/wake.rs", "test": "a_signal_from_another_thread_ends_the_wait_early"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/wake.rs", "test": "no_published_item_waits_for_the_timeout"}],
  "not_replayed": "The three lost wake-up counterexamples (mut-*) need a chosen thread schedule; no deterministic test replays them. no_published_item_waits_for_the_timeout is a two-producer stress run of the property, not a replay of an interleaving.",
  "configs": [
    {"config": "MWake-safety.cfg", "expect": "pass", "invariants": ["TypeOK", "LaneBounded", "NoLostWakeup", "NoSleepOnSignal"]},
    {"config": "MWake-safety-three-producers.cfg", "expect": "pass", "invariants": ["TypeOK", "LaneBounded", "NoLostWakeup", "NoSleepOnSignal"]},
    {"config": "MWake-liveness.cfg", "expect": "pass", "property": "EveryValueConsumed"},
